# gm-tc.tech Project Rules

⚠️ **CRITICAL**: Read "CRITICAL SAFETY RULES" section before ANY destructive operations!

## Project Overview
- **Website**: gm-tc.tech
- **Hosting**: Uberspace (U7)
- **Deployment**: Git pull from GitHub/GitLab
- **Stack**: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, PHP (CMS backend)

## Code Style

### General
- No redundant functions or methods
- DRY (Don't Repeat Yourself)
- Meaningful variable/function names
- Comment complex logic only

### HTML
- Semantic HTML5 elements
- Proper heading hierarchy
- Accessibility attributes (ARIA, alt text)

### CSS
- BEM naming convention
- Mobile-first responsive design
- CSS custom properties for theming
- No !important unless absolutely necessary

### JavaScript
- ES6+ syntax
- Vanilla JS preferred over frameworks
- Async/await for asynchronous code
- Descriptive error handling

### PHP (CMS)
- PSR-12 coding standard
- Prepared statements for DB queries
- Input validation on all user data

## Skills Reference

For detailed context, reference these skill files:

| Skill | When to Use |
|-------|-------------|
| `skills/web-design/SKILL.md` | Frontend, UI, styling, layouts |
| `skills/cms-development/SKILL.md` | Backend, database, API, auth |
| `skills/git-workflow/SKILL.md` | Version control, branching, commits |
| `skills/uberspace-deployment/SKILL.md` | Server config, deployment |
| `skills/debugging/SKILL.md` | Troubleshooting, fixing bugs |
| `skills/seo-optimization/SKILL.md` | Meta tags, search, structured data |
| `skills/cursor-project/SKILL.md` | IDE setup, workspace config |

## Workflow

1. Work on `dev` branch
2. Commit with conventional messages: `type: description`
3. Test locally
4. Merge to `main` when ready
5. SSH to Uberspace and pull

